# Story 25: Skill Files (45s)
# Hook: Define agents as Markdown skill files -- version-controlled, reusable, shareable.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-25-skill-files.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 7

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- we'll create a skill file for an agent.

[00:04.0 --> 00:06.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:06.0 --> 00:08.0]
First, create a directory for your skill files.

[00:08.0 --> 00:22.0]
Write a Markdown skill file with YAML frontmatter. Name, description, and system prompt -- all in one file.

[00:22.0 --> 00:30.0]
Spawn the agent directly from the skill file. All config comes from the Markdown frontmatter.

[00:30.0 --> 00:36.0]
##agent list confirms the agent is running.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
Skill files: portable, version-controlled agent definitions.

